{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted","id":1322389,"title":"What's it like to be peak human in Exalted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-05T04:45:32-07:00","id":1322389,"title":"What's it like to be peak human in Exalted?","content":"So let's say you got something at 5. How do you show it? How do you stunt it? Or describe it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1322210#post1322210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can manage projects really well.<br /> <br /> Best example of this is probably Aria, Marena's god-blooded mother from Keychain of Creation. For canon examples... probably The Slug?<br /> <br /> Light and L from Deathnote are also probably good inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1322243#post1322243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -At the highest level, you can manage and defend an organization which is a big player in the world, or wrap such an organization led by someone else around your little finger.<br /> <br /> -You can make a chain of deals which culminates with a closed off nation selling their rarest exotic goods to you in a historic first for their nation.<br /> <br /> -You can organize the emergency evacuation of an entire city with such efficiency and thoroughness that no one gets left behind.<br /> <br /> -You always know when it is safe to bribe your way out of trouble and never pay more than you need to.<br /> <br /> -You can uncover industrial sabotage and subterfuge through sheer accounting prowess.<br /> <br /> And other similar feats.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1322239#post1322239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cut through red tape, know who to pester to get your project done. Set up an efficient organization. Maybe parse through a heavy legalese document?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/20067-ask-a-question-get-an-answer?p=1322248#post1322248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And let us never forget being really good at making and understanding a contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that's what I got for Bureaucracy 5.<br /> <br /> So what about things like Performance? Or Investigation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 07-05-2019, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T05:01:42-07:00","id":1322391,"title":"","content":"I think it's obvious for thowe who read the topic your examples come from but you should remind newcomers these are examples about Bureaucracy 5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T11:23:00-07:00","id":1322460,"title":"","content":"I would say that the main aspect of having an Attribute or Ability at 5 is, fundamentally, that you have a pretty good shot at succeeding on difficulty 4 or 5 actions with that ability, depending on what you pair it with. But it doesn\u2019t mean you can attempt superhuman feats or that the heights of that ability aren\u2019t still difficult for you.<br /> <br /> So, I don\u2019t necessarily agree with all of those Bureaucracy examples you gave above, as some of them sound more like things you might want charms to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Investigation 5 <br /> <br /> After examining the crime scene, you can spot when all but the very best criminals have tried to clean up after themselves and usually get at least some idea of what they were trying to hide. If they didn\u2019t try to hide anything, you can probably come up with a general description of the perpetrator to hand to the constabulary.<br /> <br /> After observing someone for a few minutes, you can make an assessment as to who they are, where they come from, whether they\u2019re pretending to be someone else, and so on and you\u2019re right much more often than you\u2019re wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T02:31:10-07:00","id":1322723,"title":"","content":"You are Batman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T02:36:40-07:00","id":1322727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322723#post1322723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are Batman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. <br /> <br /> But Batman is bullshit. Especially with 'prep time'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T02:46:17-07:00","id":1322730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322727#post1322727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. <br /> <br /> But Batman is bullshit. Especially with 'prep time'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand by what I said.<br /> <br /> Batman is the single greatest example of &quot;peak human&quot;. If Batman could do it, you can do it. And a 2-die stunt is your &quot;prep time&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T02:46:39-07:00","id":1322731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322727#post1322727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Batman is bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful, them's fighting words. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T02:55:28-07:00","id":1322732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322731#post1322731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Careful, them's fighting words. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nah he's kinda right.<br /> <br /> The stuff Batman pulls out at the 11th hour (shark repellent) is incredulous bullshit. Batman is an interesting and nuanced character, but his feats are absolutely unbelievable. And they cross so many different fields that it becomes ridiculous.<br /> <br /> But that's Exalted.<br /> <br /> Whilst Batman's feats are massively out of place for the DC universe (how many times has he had a fist fight with Superman), they're right at home with what you can do with a 5 dot ability in Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T03:35:02-07:00","id":1322736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322731#post1322731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Careful, them's fighting words. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Batman's no badass normal. He's a night caste with specializations with athletics and stealth.<br /> <br /> He also sucks compared to guys like superman and the Flash. Who are the real heroes.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T04:39:34-07:00","id":1322742,"title":"","content":"I think attributes need to be considered here. they complicate matters such that you can't simply say &quot;at x dots in an ability you can do y&quot;.<br /> <br /> Someone with 5 dots in an ability and one dot in the associated attribute is going to succeed on the same tasks as someone with one dot in the ability and five dots in the same attribute. What will differ is the <i>manner</i> in which these successes manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T04:41:06-07:00","id":1322743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322742#post1322742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think attributes need to be considered here. they complicate matters such that you can't simply say &quot;at x dots in an ability you can do y&quot;.<br /> <br /> Someone with 5 dots in an ability and one dot in the associated attribute is going to succeed on the same tasks as someone with one dot in the ability and five dots in the same attribute. What will differ is the <i>manner</i> in which these successes manifest.</div> </div> </div> </div>13 dice in total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T05:30:12-07:00","id":1322750,"title":"","content":"You don\u2019t get thirteen dice on Attribute+Ability rolls in Ex3, save for when you roll out stunts and magic.<br /> <br /> (Attack pools are another matter, but even those don\u2019t get *much* higher.)<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322736#post1322736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's a night caste with specializations with athletics and stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already established pretty firmly in the past that you can play any Caste of Solar as Batman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322736#post1322736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He also sucks compared to guys like superman and the Flash. Who are the real heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sure you\u2019re being facetious here, but all things considered, it doesn\u2019t especially matter if you\u2019re a science experiment gone awry, an alien, a god, or a billionaire - there\u2019s better ways to make the world a better place than punching people in the face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-07-2019, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T05:34:37-07:00","id":1322752,"title":"","content":"13 dice is 11 with a stunt. Technically peak mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T05:43:07-07:00","id":1322754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322750#post1322750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already established pretty firmly in the past that you can play any Caste of Solar as Batman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I miss something, or did they remove the 'suppress anima' power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T06:04:02-07:00","id":1322758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322750#post1322750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already established pretty firmly in the past that you can play any Caste of Solar as Batman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zenith?<br /> <br /> The others I can all see (some fit better than others, but they can all fit). But Zenith doesn't quite work to me. I mean, obviously you can do it, but it seems a bit forced compared to the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T06:06:38-07:00","id":1322759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322460#post1322460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I don\u2019t necessarily agree with all of those Bureaucracy examples you gave above, as some of them sound more like things you might want charms to accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the examples listed are all possible with very high rolls (which excellencies can do).<br /> <br /> I think a lot of them are &quot;you can&quot; which means it's possible, not that you'll always succeed. I think that's an important point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T06:21:40-07:00","id":1322766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322759#post1322759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the examples listed are all possible with very high rolls (which excellencies can do).<br /> <br /> I think a lot of them are &amp;quot;you can&amp;quot; which means it's possible, not that you'll always succeed. I think that's an important point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellencies don't say much. <br /> <br /> When you say that, do you mean 10 dice, or 20 dice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T06:36:46-07:00","id":1322770,"title":"","content":"I mean that most of them are probably difficulty 3-5, and difficulty 5 is challenging for a human with an ability at 5. But not for a Solar with ability 5 using an excellency.<br /> I think organising an evacuation of an entire city such that no-one (including stubborn old ladies who live on their own and are too deaf to hear evacuation orders) is left behind, might be something rated higher than 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T06:41:34-07:00","id":1322771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322770#post1322770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that most of them are probably difficulty 3-5, and difficulty 5 is challenging for a human with an ability at 5. But not for a Solar with ability 5 using an excellency.<br /> I think organising an evacuation of an entire city such that no-one (including stubborn old ladies who live on their own and are too deaf to hear evacuation orders) is left behind, might be something rated higher than 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone with a 5 in that ability, with several assistants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T06:42:15-07:00","id":1322772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322770#post1322770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that most of them are probably difficulty 3-5, and difficulty 5 is challenging for a human with an ability at 5. But not for a Solar with ability 5 using an excellency.<br /> I think organising an evacuation of an entire city such that no-one (including stubborn old ladies who live on their own and are too deaf to hear evacuation orders) is left behind, might be something rated higher than 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which reminds me. You said evacuation. In what time frame?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T07:10:00-07:00","id":1322777,"title":"","content":"It was Epitome's example, not mine; so I think it depends. That's why I said it might be very difficult, or it might be fairly easy. There's all sorts of factors.<br /> I'm also not sure if successfully getting every single person out of the city is something you should be able to do with a Bureaucracy roll; it depends partially on the rolls of your subordinates, after all. Still, I'd probably declare it happened if someone rolled a ton of successes, just to make the player feel pleased with themselves. From a plot perspective, evacuating 99% of a city's population and 100% are not really very different, so it doesn't make much difference to me as ST.<br /> <br /> I have to say, I find it more practical from a game-running perspective to look at what is a certain difficulty than what someone can do with Ability 5; after all, they're rolling their Attributes as well (which, for Solars, tend to be lower than their Abilities; most low-xp Solars/Dragonblood have Abilties at 5 in several different areas, possibly 7 if they've really optimised, but have 0-1 Attributes at 5), and excellencies (which vary by Exalt-type) make a massive difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T07:34:53-07:00","id":1322779,"title":"","content":"The most elite real world experts, the peoples whose names are almost synonymous with their expertise (your Einsteins and Beethovens) of a given field would probably only rate 4 dots and a specialty.<br /> <br /> Exalted is a game about the mythic heroes, where even mortals are capable of astounding feats. Probably the biggest defining element of being Peak in a skill is in breadth, consistency, and the degree of complication that can be managed.<br /> <br /> Here a few examples off the top of my head. <hr /><br /> <b>Archery</b><br /> <br /> A renowned Archer who is talented enough to be renowned across the lands (who is likely to Dex 4, Archery 4 with a specialty) can reliably hit a moving target at 200 meters.<br /> <br /> A peak Archer (Dex 5, Archery 5 with a specialty) can also reliably hit the moving target, but can do so even under duress or in bad conditions (high winds, bad lighting, while wounded, etc).<br /> <br /> An Exalted Archer, backed by charms and excellencies, can make shots that should be impossible even with less than peak base die pools. The Renowned Archer Exalts, and can now hit things at 300 yards with ease with arrows made of light and essence that set the target on fire. <hr /><br /> <b>Athletics</b><br /> <br /> A renowned Athlete (Athletics 4 with a 4 or 5 in one of their Physical Attributes and a specialty in their favored endeavor) has probably never lost a contest in multiple events. No one within leagues is faster or stronger. The perform at levels that would humble most real world decathletes.<br /> <br /> A peak Athlete (Athletics 5 with at least one Physical Attribute at 5 dots) is the person who wanders into town after town challenging their renowned local champions and beating them. They can maintain their performance under duress (swimming in frigid waters, climbing a cliff in driving rain, hoisting a heavy load one-handed).<br /> <br /> An Exalted Athlete can perform at superhuman levels, overpowering bulls and outrunning horses, leaving even talented opponents looking slow and feeble in comparison. <hr /><br /> <b>Awareness</b><br /> <br /> An individual renowned for their Awareness(Awareness 4) might garner a nickname like &quot;Hawk&quot; or &quot;Bloodhound&quot;. They can identify subtle ingredients in a meal by taste or smell, read fine text at range, and hear the creak of floorboards on the other side of the house.<br /> <br /> An individual at peak Awareness can do all of the above but under more difficult conditions. They can identify subtle ingredients beneath overpowering spices, read fine text at range in bad lighting, and hear the floorboards creak over the din of a raucous party.<br /> <br /> An individual at Exalted Awareness can taste<br /> what cooking implements the preparer used when they made the meal, read fine text at range in the dark, and hear floorboards creak at their neighbors house during a party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T07:57:50-07:00","id":1322781,"title":"","content":"Ability 4+Specialty is the same number of dice as Ability 5 in that area, so I don't see any difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T08:00:13-07:00","id":1322782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322758#post1322758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zenith?<br /> <br /> The others I can all see (some fit better than others, but they can all fit). But Zenith doesn't quite work to me. I mean, obviously you can do it, but it seems a bit forced compared to the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman-as-Zenith would be the magnetic figure who's simultaneously an inspiration to his allies and a terror to his enemies, an unbreakable pillar of athleticism and physicality that weathers constant abuse - physical, mental, and otherwise - with the unflinching resolve of a statue.<br /> <br /> \u200bCaste Abilities include Athletics, Integrity, Presence, Resistance, and Survival. Probably goes with Presence Supernal with an eye for early acquisition of Terrifying Apparition of Glory and the various underling-uplifting Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-07-2019, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T08:13:56-07:00","id":1322784,"title":"","content":"Ah, that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T08:37:52-07:00","id":1322791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322784#post1322784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, that works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't being flippant; I've given this plenty of thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-07-2019, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T09:09:25-07:00","id":1322795,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure, you mentioned you'd talked about it previously, but I didn't remember that so was interested to see your explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T10:29:22-07:00","id":1322986,"title":"","content":"Awesome. What about war? Can they pull off the insane, like Japan or Germany winning the war?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T13:07:05-07:00","id":1323035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322986#post1322986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome. What about war? Can they pull off the insane, like Japan or Germany winning the war?</div> </div> </div> </div>They approach war like Ender/Andrew Wiggin. They're able to extrapolate and visualize how others will react. They'll have contingencies. They'll know absolutely when you need to sacrifice life, and when to pull back. In the study of your opposition, their tactics, you truly get to know them. And then you know how to beat them. <br /> <br /> A lot would have to do with psychology. It's more than just troop management. It is the planning, it having the spy network in place, it is looking where you are weak and beefing that up. <br /> <br /> So combine Xanatos (Gargoyles, known for Xanatos gambit) and Ender Wiggin, and you get those who pull of the insane. You get a leader who inspires troops on the other side to join with him. You get someone who is able to enact psychological warfare as well as physical warfare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T13:49:40-07:00","id":1323045,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I'd argue a lot of the Nazis' failures were political, intelligence or industrial, rather than military.<br /> <br /> But were I to run WW2 as a game, Operation Sealion would probably be a War roll (honestly we won due to better bureaucracy, but I'd probably just give us a bonus on their war roll), and if the Nazis had succeeded on that, Britain would probably have signed an armistice, which would make a US invasion of western Europe untenable. A successful high-difficulty war roll would probably be less beat the Russians, and more know that invading Russia is a terrible idea so don't.<br /> <br /> One issue my friend has complained about while running a game with PCs with high bureaucracy and war is they sometimes want to do things that don't work, and think they should be able to because of their high ability; rather, it will make them realise that it just won't work.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there's a lot of variables that could have changed, and it's difficult to tell how much difference it would have made. There's also the question of what &quot;victory&quot; is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T14:33:27-07:00","id":1323054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1322730#post1322730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I stand by what I said.<br /> <br /> Batman is the single greatest example of &quot;peak human&quot;. If Batman could do it, you can do it. And a 2-die stunt is your &quot;prep time&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doc Savage is a better example of Peak Human in my opinion, and he came out BEFORE Batman (IIRC) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 07-08-2019, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T15:13:30-07:00","id":1323065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323045#post1323045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue my friend has complained about while running a game with PCs with high bureaucracy and war is they sometimes want to do things that don't work, and think they should be able to because of their high ability; rather, it will make them realise that it just won't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of 'Rule of Cool' in Exalted - you can just as rightly state that someone with high Martial Arts wouldn't practice animal styles that IRL are totally going to make folk who understand what works well in real MMA unarmed combat and why it works cringe... but it's a conceit of setting that they do work well for mortals, even before you get to the Exalted's magic.<br /> <br /> I mean, an Exalted where the mortal and Exalted heroes of legend, able to do things which to us are the impossible tropes of legend in their melodramatic kung fu sort of world, have the power of realizing that those don't actually work and instead not doing them... would be a different thing! (At the risk of straying into sarcasm that I don't want).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T00:38:30-07:00","id":1323139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323045#post1323045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue my friend has complained about while running a game with PCs with high bureaucracy and war is they sometimes want to do things that don't work, and think they should be able to because of their high ability; rather, it will make them realise that it just won't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who has two thumbs,<br /> And hurled up the sky,<br /> When you were waddling yay-high?<br /> This guy!<br /> <br /> Exalted is a game of mythic fantasy. In real life, arrows fly in curves. In mythic fantasy heroes can shoot arrows through a dozen axes. In mythic fantasy, mortals can engage in games of skill and wit with the avatars of death (or woo them with their great musical skill).<br /> <br /> 5s put you at peak ability in a world of mythic fantasy. In real life, a world class sprinter is not a world class weightlifter. In Exalted, Athletics 5 means you're both. Likewise being a history buff doesn't make you an electrical engineering expert... unless you're Batman.<br /> <br /> Your feats have to be plausible within the context of being a mythic hero. I'd allow characters with 5 Athletics to sprint at 30 mph then jump 8' straight up into the air because both feats are plausible within the scope of peak human ability. But you're not running a mile in two minutes or high-jumping 20' without charms, no matter how well you roll.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if your Bureaucracy/War project would be plausible within a mythic narrative like the Odyessy or Lysistrata, then I'd allow it without stressing too much about the possibility of it working In Real Life. If you want to put a weapon in the hand of every man, woman and child in Zion and march them into that dock, then roll against Difficulty 5. If the menfolk of the Realm have a cunning plan to bring about peace with Lookshy, then make that roll to lay down your burden. This doesn't let you raise an army of hundreds from a population of dozens. To do the flat out impossible, you need charms.<br /> <br /> Lots of stuff in Exalted (like Martial Arts) <i>shouldn't</i> work. You shouldn't be able to remove someone's appendix in the dark during a hurricane without proper medical tools. But Exalted allows you to try. <br /> <br /> I would allow Bureaucracy/War projects unless they were incredibly outlandish (like trying to siege a city with seven men walking around the wall blowing trumpets or trying to build a bridge from Lookshy to Skullstone).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-09-2019, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T03:25:12-07:00","id":1323159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323045#post1323045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue my friend has complained about while running a game with PCs with high bureaucracy and war is they sometimes want to do things that don't work, and think they should be able to because of their high ability; rather, it will make them realise that it just won't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the rule of cool, and then there is the rule of stupid. And the rule of stupid often supercedes the rule of cool. Backstabbing Russia and engaging in a two front war is not cool. It is stupid. Especially as you don't plan for your troops being in Russia in the winter. Among other things. <br /> <br /> If you let ego get in the way of War and Bureau 5, then nothing is going to save you if you overextend yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T08:46:49-07:00","id":1323204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323159#post1323159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's the rule of cool, and then there is the rule of stupid. And the rule of stupid often supercedes the rule of cool. Backstabbing Russia and engaging in a two front war is not cool. It is stupid. Especially as you don't plan for your troops being in Russia in the winter. Among other things. </div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of the classic blunders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T08:55:31-07:00","id":1323206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323204#post1323204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one of the classic blunders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hitler: &quot;Inconceivable!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T08:58:59-07:00","id":1323207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323206#post1323206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hitler: &amp;quot;Inconceivable!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah. Hitler. <br /> <br /> When you suddenly realize you've picked a fight with half the world. <br /> <br /> Always wondered what would have happened if he had Exalted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T09:03:28-07:00","id":1323209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323207#post1323207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah. Hitler. <br /> <br /> When you suddenly realize you've picked a fight with half the world. <br /> <br /> Always wondered what would have happened if he had Exalted...</div> </div> </div> </div>Been there, played that.<br /> <br /> Hitler as a Zenith is surprisingly more fun than Hitler as a Fiend or Hitler as a Dynast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T09:05:17-07:00","id":1323211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323209#post1323209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Been there, played that.<br /> <br /> Hitler as a Zenith is surprisingly more fun than Hitler as a Fiend or Hitler as a Dynast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? <br /> <br /> I was always wondering about those comments from his generals. Was he a truly smart general, put down by drugs? Or did they succeed despite him? <br /> <br /> What would fighting a war supernal even be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T09:58:15-07:00","id":1323220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323139#post1323139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who has two thumbs,<br /> And hurled up the sky,<br /> When you were waddling yay-high?<br /> This guy!<br /> <br /> Exalted is a game of mythic fantasy. In real life, arrows fly in curves. In mythic fantasy heroes can shoot arrows through a dozen axes. In mythic fantasy, mortals can engage in games of skill and wit with the avatars of death (or woo them with their great musical skill).<br /> <br /> 5s put you at peak ability in a world of mythic fantasy. In real life, a world class sprinter is not a world class weightlifter. In Exalted, Athletics 5 means you're both. Likewise being a history buff doesn't make you an electrical engineering expert... unless you're Batman.<br /> <br /> Your feats have to be plausible within the context of being a mythic hero. I'd allow characters with 5 Athletics to sprint at 30 mph then jump 8' straight up into the air because both feats are plausible within the scope of peak human ability. But you're not running a mile in two minutes or high-jumping 20' without charms, no matter how well you roll.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if your Bureaucracy/War project would be plausible within a mythic narrative like the Odyessy or Lysistrata, then I'd allow it without stressing too much about the possibility of it working In Real Life. If you want to put a weapon in the hand of every man, woman and child in Zion and march them into that dock, then roll against Difficulty 5. If the menfolk of the Realm have a cunning plan to bring about peace with Lookshy, then make that roll to lay down your burden. This doesn't let you raise an army of hundreds from a population of dozens. To do the flat out impossible, you need charms.<br /> <br /> Lots of stuff in Exalted (like Martial Arts) <i>shouldn't</i> work. You shouldn't be able to remove someone's appendix in the dark during a hurricane without proper medical tools. But Exalted allows you to try.<br /> <br /> I would allow Bureaucracy/War projects unless they were incredibly outlandish (like trying to siege a city with seven men walking around the wall blowing trumpets or trying to build a bridge from Lookshy to Skullstone).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what he meant is that, even with 2 people that accepts participating in a mythic setting with mythic rules, it's hard to have the same expectations of what should fall in the territory of Charms and what should not, and that high level ability would sometimes tell the character &quot;Well I can't do this without a Charm because it's too hard&quot;.<br /> <br /> To reuse one of your examples, put a weapon in the hand of every man, woman and child in Zion and march them into that dock (btw I don't know Zion so i'm going to assume it's a city big enough to make things complicated and there is a dock nearby you want to invade) could be a Difficulty 4-5 roll, but what if there are no weapons in Zion and the character wants them to have battle-ready weapons? Does a good roll simulates the fact every capable blacksmith is gonna forge one on its command, or should that be a Charm that inspired people to find their antique family weapons ? What if there are extreme taboos in Zion that men don't fight, should a War/Bureaucracy roll allow to bypass that ? Or is it a Charm ? What if the people at the dock are the close family of the rebels you are trying to inspire in Zion, it seems it would be the territory of a Charm to force a wem and women to attack their sisters and brothers in a global rebellion, but maybe a roll would do ? What if the players want the rebels to be ready in one night, and the ST thinks it can only be achieved in one week ?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I have the answers to these questions. I'm trying to say that if you take 2 different players, and ask them if they think it deserves a Charm or if just a good roll is enough because it falls into what humans are capable of, you will have different answers, all motivated by different analysis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T10:17:58-07:00","id":1323224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323211#post1323211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? <br /> <br /> I was always wondering about those comments from his generals. Was he a truly smart general, put down by drugs? Or did they succeed despite him? <br /> <br /> What would fighting a war supernal even be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was a bad general, partly because he wasn't actually a trained general, partly because he was on drugs, partly because he was arrogant and couldn't admit that any failures of the German war machine could be due to his decisions, and partly because of his massive racism; he believed the Russians were Untermensch and thus their soldiers would be rubbish compared to the German soldiers, when of course they were not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T10:24:51-07:00","id":1323228,"title":"","content":"Overall, I'd give Hitler about War 2.<br /> <br /> But it's important to remember that early in the war the German forces weren't commanded by Hitler, but by a number of skilled generals who used innovative new tactics and outmanoeuvred the French. <br /> But the allies of course also had very good generals, amphibious assaults are incredibly difficult (why do you think Taiwan is free?) so the British generals (plus Churchill, who had a lot more military command experience than Hitler) successfully defended, and then invading Russia meant that the Germans were badly outnumbered, which got worse when America joined (which wasn't even Hitler's mistake, it was his allies).<br /> <br /> This is why I said War 5 might have won the Fascists the War, but not definitely; remember that the allies had brilliant generals too, plus more men.<br /> <br /> Actually, one of the PCs in a game I play is basically Djala Hitler as a Dawn with War 5 and every War charm.<br /> And he is brilliant at battles, but so far he hasn't achieved his dream of a Greater Djala Dominion because, essentially, he's terrible at making allies on account of being a fascist. His men are constantly deserting due to poor morale, he's put down multiple rebellions and coup attempts, started a pointless war with the group who'd make the best allies, his people are starving, etc.<br /> None of this is due to poor military skills, it's due to poor diplomacy, intelligence, and just generally being a tyrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-09-2019, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T10:37:55-07:00","id":1323230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323228#post1323228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I said War 5 might have won the Fascists the War, but not definitely; remember that the allies had brilliant generals too, plus more men.</div> </div> </div> </div>And leaders who didn't call <i>factual information they happened to not like</i> &quot;L\u00fcgenpresse.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, they didn't <i>then</i>, anyway.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, yeah, just because a guy's smart and talented, even perhaps magically so, it doesn't mean he's actually gonna be placed in an influential position, if the guy in charge is more interested in surrounding himself with people who tell him what he wants to hear, competence be damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-09-2019, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T13:57:07-07:00","id":1323275,"title":"","content":"Certainly. This was one of the reasons Hitler was such a poor overall commander.<br /> <br /> But I took it from Accelerator's point that the overall commander (so, I guess Hitler) was the one with War 5, and while you could argue about it, I'll assume that would mean a good enough understanding of War to be able to tell what was true and what was not.<br /> (Still, there's a question of how well high ratings in knowledge-based abilities clash with ideology. Like, if you're a communist with Bureaucracy 5, do you know that the poor performance of a centralised command economy run entirely by humans in a huge country is not due to American saboteurs and class traitors? I'd argue that Lenin's NEP is proof that you do know, but there's arguments against as well.)<br /> <br /> After all, the traditional* view of German generalship is that they did, in fact, have one of the greatest commanders in the world (ie War 5, or at least 4 with a +1 specialty in Tanks or Desert Warfare) at their disposal, but that he was overruled by senior generals with more traditional views of tactics, and eventually Hitler forced him to kill himself (though tbh, at that point they'd already lost).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Though obviously many revisionists now claim this is part of our rehabilitation of Germany post-war in order to fight the Commies. But anyway. He certainly was a very able commander, even if not quite the chivalrous liberal we Brits and the US liked to paint him. His strategy for defending France probably was better than Rundstedt's, but he did make the same mistake of believing our attack would be at Calais, when in fact it was at Normandy. I guess this is less due to strategy and more due to our spies being better than the Nazi spies, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T20:24:31-07:00","id":1323354,"title":"","content":"John McClane, James Bond, Jason Bourne, and John WIck come to mind as characters in their worlds hwo are considered &quot;peak human&quot; but do a lot of stuff that would probably actually kill/not be possible for real people. I tend to go with an idea that in Creation a lot of things that are bullshit movie physics are the kind sof things Solars are pulling, as bullshit movie physics often goes with the idea that &quot;If you were this good you could do it too.&quot;<br /> <br /> Probably often goes beyond some of them, but I fully admit I watch more movies than read comic books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T22:21:23-07:00","id":1323377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323354#post1323354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">John McClane, James Bond, Jason Bourne, and John WIck come to mind as characters in their worlds hwo are considered &quot;peak human&quot; but do a lot of stuff that would probably actually kill/not be possible for real people. I tend to go with an idea that in Creation a lot of things that are bullshit movie physics are the kind sof things Solars are pulling, as bullshit movie physics often goes with the idea that &quot;If you were this good you could do it too.&quot;<br /> <br /> Probably often goes beyond some of them, but I fully admit I watch more movies than read comic books.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of their stuff is also luck based, so...maybe that could represent stunts? I know it's dicey saying that stunts are a real in game thing that happens, but it might explain how they consistently pull off stuff that's just barely plausible without being dead after their second mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T08:44:09-07:00","id":1323450,"title":"","content":"For peak war humans, I'd consider Andrew/Ender Wiggin, Bean, and maybe Petra to be peak humans in that regard. Where they're able to extrapolate and internalize war, considering all the angles. Knowing when to move on, knowing when to strike. Knowing about weaknesses in supply lines and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T10:50:09-07:00","id":1323470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323220#post1323220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what he meant is that, even with 2 people that accepts participating in a mythic setting with mythic rules, it's hard to have the same expectations of what should fall in the territory of Charms and what should not, and that high level ability would sometimes tell the character &amp;quot;Well I can't do this without a Charm because it's too hard&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> To reuse one of your examples, put a weapon in the hand of every man, woman and child in Zion and march them into that dock (btw I don't know Zion so i'm going to assume it's a city big enough to make things complicated and there is a dock nearby you want to invade) could be a Difficulty 4-5 roll, but what if there are no weapons in Zion and the character wants them to have battle-ready weapons? Does a good roll simulates the fact every capable blacksmith is gonna forge one on its command, or should that be a Charm that inspired people to find their antique family weapons ? What if there are extreme taboos in Zion that men don't fight, should a War/Bureaucracy roll allow to bypass that ? Or is it a Charm ? What if the people at the dock are the close family of the rebels you are trying to inspire in Zion, it seems it would be the territory of a Charm to force a wem and women to attack their sisters and brothers in a global rebellion, but maybe a roll would do ? What if the players want the rebels to be ready in one night, and the ST thinks it can only be achieved in one week ?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I have the answers to these questions. I'm trying to say that if you take 2 different players, and ask them if they think it deserves a Charm or if just a good roll is enough because it falls into what humans are capable of, you will have different answers, all motivated by different analysis.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case Zion is the last human city locked in total war with a race that wants to annihilate mankind, but I guess my pop culture references are a little dated.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree with your point though.<br /> <br /> My inclination is to go with the drama. Which usually means supporting player agency and saying &quot;yes, and&quot;, but if the players are trying to sidestep the story then I have no problem in telling them that what they are trying to do is impossible, but I'd do it with a &quot;no, but&quot;.<br /> <br /> No, you can't put a gun in the hands of every man, woman and child in Zion and march them into that dock. But you can have the entire APU Corp and half the infantry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T11:25:21-07:00","id":1323483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323470#post1323470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case Zion is the last human city locked in total war with a race that wants to annihilate mankind, but I guess my pop culture references are a little dated.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree with your point though.<br /> <br /> My inclination is to go with the drama. Which usually means supporting player agency and saying &quot;yes, and&quot;, but if the players are trying to sidestep the story then I have no problem in telling them that what they are trying to do is impossible, but I'd do it with a &quot;no, but&quot;.<br /> <br /> No, you can't put a gun in the hands of every man, woman and child in Zion and march them into that dock. But you can have the entire APU Corp and half the infantry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are we talking about the matrix city Zion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T11:46:05-07:00","id":1323489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322389-what-s-it-like-to-be-peak-human-in-exalted?p=1323483#post1323483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are we talking about the matrix city Zion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I was kinda hoping people would riff off the Lysistrata reference but I admit that one is even more dated. (Get it? No? I'll be over here...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T13:25:23-07:00","id":1323501,"title":"","content":"No Matirx is fine I was just thinking &quot;Well that could totally be a name for some Exalted city I don't know about&quot; and I didn't even think it could be related to another pop-culture reference, don't worry you are not &quot;dated&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T14:16:27-07:00","id":1323519,"title":"","content":"I assumed it was, you know, Jerusalem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}